0010: a single-channel format does not argue about channel order.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: not sent separately - part of
the ADR-0003 family (requires 0005).
**Found:** exactly two of the 72 vkd3d format classes went linear on
stock, both of them vkd3d's most common list for a 32-bit texture.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. Typeless-BGRA8 textures with a UAV view (the D3D11 typed-UAV rule
appends `R32{U,I,F}`) stop losing the tiling on gen2.

## Summary

`tu6_format_list_swaps_are_uniform()` required every format's swap to match, and
the appended `R32_*` carries `WZYX` against BGRA8's `WXYZ`. But on tiling no swap
for a view exists at all: `fd6_pipe2swap()` returns `WZYX` to every format except
`is_mutable` (`fd6_format_table.c:396`), so the disagreement has no
representation and cannot be why the image demotes. The patch excludes
single-channel formats from the channel-order comparison (they have no channel
order); block shape, channel count, swizzle and channel sizes stay checked for
everyone.

## Evidence

Four hunks in `tu_formats.cc`. Enumeration: `scripts/fmt-list-gate-check.py
--exp-9` - no vkd3d class on gen2 goes linear any more. On hardware, BGRA8 fill
and readback through the image's own format stay EXACT 0/262144.

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| the two linear classes | `scripts/fmt-list-gate-check.py --exp-9`, journal 21 | both tiled |
| the base view still reads correctly | BGRA8 fill/readback, journal 21 | EXACT 0/262144 |
| what the patch costs | `R32_UINT` view over the same memory, journal 21 | 261120/262144 words byte-swapped vs linear - inexpressible in D3D12 (typed UAV load returns float4) |
| nothing else moves | the 94-row matrix, journal 24.3 | 94 EXACT |

## The change in this repo

The cross-order `{BGRA8, RGBA8}` list and NV12 must stay linear - there the
disagreement is real. Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name explicit
(without 0005 it does not apply).

## Related

Requires `0005`; `0006` (same table family); ADR-0003.

